    "created_at": "2026-10-13T07:00:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-13T07:00:29Z",
    "body": "> 3\\. > Fullscreen inside of `<frame>` should have been forbidden by the \"allowed to use\" algorithm anyway.\n>         \n>         Right, but it [used to work](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/32a059337eb1c538242091adc170c41be325443b), is all, which just means that whatever the problem is in Gecko probably doesn't apply to Chromium. I'm still fine with not allowing it.\n\nIt seems this relies on Permissions-Policy, but I don't see where it forbids document in frame specifically.\n\nI was looking at this old WebKit bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=95402\n\nAnd \"fullscreen inside a frame\" works in Safari https://people.igalia.com/fwang/webkit-bug-95402/frameset.html (served with `Permissions-Policy: fullscreen=*`) but not in Firefox or Chrome.\n\nThe following \"fullscreen inside an iframe\" works in the three browsers: https://people.igalia.com/fwang/webkit-bug-95402/iframe.html (again served with `Permissions-Policy: fullscreen=*`).\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
